        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Hold a PPL and SPL? EASA and FAA? NinerLog handles them all. Flights count toward all applicable licenses and class ratings automatically.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Any regulatory authority worldwide</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Class ratings with expiry tracking (SEP, MEP, TMG, IR)</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">No per-license flight assignment &mdash; flights count everywhere</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

